window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-434ee24ee096022e"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"use-codex-in-linear\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"linear-codex\">在 Linear 中使用 Codex</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取 Markdown 版本的文档。</p> </blockquote> <p>你可以在 Linear 的 issue（任务/问题单）中委派工作给 Codex：把 issue 指派给 Codex，或在评论中提及 <code>@Codex</code>。Codex 会创建一个云端聊天，并在其中回复进度和结果。</p> <p>Codex for Linear 面向付费方案提供（请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-24e0a6ab1e90e5b7\">定价</a>）。</p> <p>如果你使用 Enterprise 方案，请联系 ChatGPT 工作区管理员，让其在<a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/admin/settings\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">工作区设置（需联网）</a>中启用 Codex 云端聊天，并在<a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/admin/ca\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">连接器设置（需联网）</a>中启用 <strong>Codex for Linear</strong>。</p> <p><a id=\"set-up-the-linear-integration\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"linear\">设置 Linear 集成</h2> <ol> <li>设置 <a href=\"#/article/a-c302e8415c7f61ad\">Codex 云端聊天</a>：在 <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/codex\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Codex（需联网）</a> 中连接 GitHub，并为你希望 Codex 使用的代码仓库创建一个<a href=\"#/article/a-73011d6801bc30d3\">环境</a>。</li> <li>前往 <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/codex/settings/connectors\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Codex 设置（需联网）</a>，为你的工作区安装 <strong>Codex for Linear</strong>。</li> <li>在 Linear issue 的评论串中提及 <code>@Codex</code>，以关联你的 Linear 账户。</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"delegate-work-to-codex\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"codex\">委派工作给 Codex</h2> <p>有两种委派方式：</p> <p><a id=\"assign-an-issue-to-codex\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"issue-codex\">将 issue 指派给 Codex</h3> <p>安装集成后，你可以像将 issue 指派给队友一样，将 issue 指派给 Codex。Codex 会开始处理，并在该 issue 中发布进度更新。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：将 Codex 指派给 Linear issue</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"mention-codex-in-comments\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"codex_1\">在评论中提及 <code>@Codex</code></h3> <p>你也可以在评论串中提及 <code>@Codex</code>，以委派工作或提问。Codex 回复后，你可以在同一个评论串中继续跟进，从而延续同一段聊天。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：在 Linear issue 评论中提及 Codex</p> </blockquote> <p>Codex 开始处理 issue 后，会<a href=\"#/article/a-434ee24ee096022e?anchor=how-codex-chooses-an-environment-and-repo\">选择一个环境和代码仓库</a>来开展工作。 如果要指定某个代码仓库，请在评论中写明，例如：<code>@Codex fix this in openai/codex</code>。</p> <p>查看进度的方法：</p> <ul> <li>在 issue 中打开 <strong>Activity（活动）</strong>，查看进度更新。</li> <li>打开聊天链接，查看更多处理细节。</li> </ul> <p>Codex 完成后，会发布摘要和已完成聊天的链接，你可以据此创建拉取请求。</p> <p><a id=\"how-codex-chooses-an-environment-and-repo\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"codex_2\">Codex 如何选择环境和代码仓库</h3> <ul> <li>Linear 会根据 issue 的上下文推荐代码仓库。Codex 会选择与该推荐最匹配的环境。如果请求不明确，则会退回使用你最近使用过的环境。</li> <li>聊天会针对该环境的仓库映射中列出的第一个代码仓库的默认分支运行。如果需要更换默认仓库或添加更多仓库，请在 Codex 中更新仓库映射。</li> <li>如果没有合适的环境或代码仓库，Codex 会在 Linear 中回复如何修复问题，然后再重试。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"automatically-assign-issues-to-codex\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"issue-codex_1\">自动将 issue 指派给 Codex</h2> <p>你可以使用分诊规则自动将 issue 指派给 Codex：</p> <ol> <li>在 Linear 中打开 <strong>Settings（设置）</strong>。</li> <li>在 <strong>Your teams（你的团队）</strong>下选择你的团队。</li> <li>在工作流设置中打开 <strong>Triage（分诊）</strong>并启用它。</li> <li>在 <strong>Triage rules（分诊规则）</strong>中创建规则，选择 <strong>Delegate（委派）</strong> &gt; <strong>Codex</strong>（还可以设置其他属性）。</li> </ol> <p>新 issue 进入分诊流程后，Linear 会自动将其指派给 Codex。 使用分诊规则时，Codex 会使用 issue 创建者的账户运行聊天。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：分诊规则自动将 Linear issue 指派给 Codex</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"data-usage-privacy-and-security\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">数据使用、隐私与安全</h2> <p>当你提及 <code>@Codex</code> 或将 issue 指派给 Codex 时，Codex 会接收 issue 内容，以理解你的请求并创建聊天。 数据处理遵循 OpenAI 的<a href=\"https://openai.com/privacy\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">隐私政策（需联网）</a>、<a href=\"https://openai.com/terms/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">使用条款（需联网）</a>及其他适用<a href=\"https://openai.com/policies\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">政策（需联网）</a>。 有关安全性的更多信息，请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3\">Codex 安全文档</a>。</p> <p>Codex 使用大型语言模型，可能会出错。请务必审查它的回答和差异。</p> <p><a id=\"tips-and-troubleshooting\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">提示与故障排除</h2> <ul> <li><strong>缺少连接：</strong> 如果 Codex 无法确认你的 Linear 连接状态，它会在 issue 中回复一个用于连接账户的链接。</li> <li><strong>选择了意外的环境：</strong> 在评论串中回复你想要的环境，例如 <code>@Codex please run this in openai/codex</code>。</li> <li><strong>处理的代码位置不正确：</strong> 补充更多上下文，或在 <code>@Codex</code> 评论中给出明确指令。</li> <li><strong>需要更多帮助：</strong> 请参阅 <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">OpenAI 帮助中心（需联网）</a>。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"connect-linear-for-local-tasks-mcp\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"connect-linear-for-local-work-mcp\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"linearmcp\">为本地工作连接 Linear（MCP）</h2> <p>如果你使用 ChatGPT 桌面应用、Codex CLI 或 IDE 扩展，并希望 Codex 在本地访问 Linear issue，请配置 Linear Model Context Protocol（MCP）服务器。</p> <p>更多信息请参阅 <a href=\"https://linear.app/integrations/codex-mcp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Linear MCP 文档（需联网）</a>。</p> <p>IDE 扩展和 CLI 共用同一套配置，因此 MCP 服务器的设置步骤也相同。</p> <p><a id=\"use-the-cli-recommended\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"cli\">使用 CLI（推荐）</h3> <p>如果已安装 CLI，请运行：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">codex mcp add linear --url https://mcp.linear.app/mcp\n</code></pre> <p>这会提示你使用 Linear 账户登录并将其连接到 Codex。</p> <p><a id=\"configure-manually\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_3\">手动配置</h3> <ol> <li>在编辑器中打开 <code>~/.codex/config.toml</code>。</li> <li>添加以下内容：</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">[mcp_servers.linear]\nurl = \"https://mcp.linear.app/mcp\"\n</code></pre> <ol> <li>运行 <code>codex mcp login linear</code> 登录。</li> </ol>","en":"<h1 id=\"use-codex-in-linear\">Use Codex in Linear</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Use Codex in Linear to delegate work from issues. Assign an issue to Codex or mention <code>@Codex</code> in a comment, and Codex creates a cloud chat and replies with progress and results.</p> <p>Codex in Linear is available on paid plans (see <a href=\"#/article/a-24e0a6ab1e90e5b7\">Pricing</a>).</p> <p>If you're on an Enterprise plan, ask your ChatGPT workspace admin to turn on Codex cloud chats in <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/admin/settings\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">workspace settings (online)</a> and enable <strong>Codex for Linear</strong> in <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/admin/ca\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">connector settings (online)</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"set-up-the-linear-integration\">Set up the Linear integration</h2> <ol> <li>Set up <a href=\"#/article/a-c302e8415c7f61ad\">Codex cloud chats</a> by connecting GitHub in <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/codex\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Codex (online)</a> and creating an <a href=\"#/article/a-73011d6801bc30d3\">environment</a> for the repository you want Codex to work in.</li> <li>Go to <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/codex/settings/connectors\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Codex settings (online)</a> and install <strong>Codex for Linear</strong> for your workspace.</li> <li>Link your Linear account by mentioning <code>@Codex</code> in a comment thread on a Linear issue.</li> </ol> <h2 id=\"delegate-work-to-codex\">Delegate work to Codex</h2> <p>You can delegate in two ways:</p> <h3 id=\"assign-an-issue-to-codex\">Assign an issue to Codex</h3> <p>After you install the integration, you can assign issues to Codex the same way you assign them to teammates. Codex starts work and posts updates back to the issue.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: Assigning Codex to a Linear issue</p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"mention-codex-in-comments\">Mention <code>@Codex</code> in comments</h3> <p>You can also mention <code>@Codex</code> in comment threads to delegate work or ask questions. After Codex replies, follow up in the thread to continue the same chat.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: Mentioning Codex in a Linear issue comment</p> </blockquote> <p>After Codex starts working on an issue, it <a href=\"#/article/a-434ee24ee096022e?anchor=how-codex-chooses-an-environment-and-repo\">chooses an environment and repo</a> to work in. To pin a specific repo, include it in your comment, for example: <code>@Codex fix this in openai/codex</code>.</p> <p>To track progress:</p> <ul> <li>Open <strong>Activity</strong> on the issue to see progress updates.</li> <li>Open the chat link to follow along in more detail.</li> </ul> <p>When Codex finishes, it posts a summary and a link to the completed chat so you can create a pull request.</p> <h3 id=\"how-codex-chooses-an-environment-and-repo\">How Codex chooses an environment and repo</h3> <ul> <li>Linear suggests a repository based on the issue context. Codex selects the environment that best matches that suggestion. If the request is ambiguous, it falls back to the environment you used most recently.</li> <li>The chat runs against the default branch of the first repository listed in that environment’s repo map. Update the repo map in Codex if you need a different default or more repositories.</li> <li>If no suitable environment or repository is available, Codex will reply in Linear with instructions on how to fix the issue before retrying.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"automatically-assign-issues-to-codex\">Automatically assign issues to Codex</h2> <p>You can assign issues to Codex automatically using triage rules:</p> <ol> <li>In Linear, go to <strong>Settings</strong>.</li> <li>Under <strong>Your teams</strong>, select your team.</li> <li>In the workflow settings, open <strong>Triage</strong> and turn it on.</li> <li>In <strong>Triage rules</strong>, create a rule and choose <strong>Delegate</strong> &gt; <strong>Codex</strong> (and any other properties you want to set).</li> </ol> <p>Linear assigns new issues that enter triage to Codex automatically. When you use triage rules, Codex runs chats using the account of the issue creator.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: Linear triage rule automatically assigning issues to Codex</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"data-usage-privacy-and-security\">Data usage, privacy, and security</h2> <p>When you mention <code>@Codex</code> or assign an issue to it, Codex receives your issue content to understand your request and create a chat. Data handling follows OpenAI's <a href=\"https://openai.com/privacy\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Privacy Policy (online)</a>, <a href=\"https://openai.com/terms/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Terms of Use (online)</a>, and other applicable <a href=\"https://openai.com/policies\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">policies (online)</a>. For more on security, see the <a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3\">Codex security documentation</a>.</p> <p>Codex uses large language models that can make mistakes. Always review answers and diffs.</p> <h2 id=\"tips-and-troubleshooting\">Tips and troubleshooting</h2> <ul> <li><strong>Missing connections</strong>: If Codex can't confirm your Linear connection, it replies in the issue with a link to connect your account.</li> <li><strong>Unexpected environment choice</strong>: Reply in the thread with the environment you want (for example, <code>@Codex please run this in openai/codex</code>).</li> <li><strong>Wrong part of the code</strong>: Add more context in the issue, or give explicit instructions in your <code>@Codex</code> comment.</li> <li><strong>More help</strong>: See the <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">OpenAI Help Center (online)</a>.</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"connect-linear-for-local-tasks-mcp\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"connect-linear-for-local-work-mcp\">Connect Linear for local work (MCP)</h2> <p>If you're using the ChatGPT desktop app, Codex CLI, or IDE extension and want it to access Linear issues locally, configure the Linear Model Context Protocol (MCP) server.</p> <p>To learn more, <a href=\"https://linear.app/integrations/codex-mcp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">check out the Linear MCP docs (online)</a>.</p> <p>The setup steps for the MCP server are the same regardless of whether you use the IDE extension or the CLI since both share the same configuration.</p> <h3 id=\"use-the-cli-recommended\">Use the CLI (recommended)</h3> <p>If you have the CLI installed, run:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">codex mcp add linear --url https://mcp.linear.app/mcp\n</code></pre> <p>This prompts you to sign in with your Linear account and connect it to Codex.</p> <h3 id=\"configure-manually\">Configure manually</h3> <ol> <li>Open <code>~/.codex/config.toml</code> in your editor.</li> <li>Add the following:</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">[mcp_servers.linear]\nurl = \"https://mcp.linear.app/mcp\"\n</code></pre> <ol> <li>Run <code>codex mcp login linear</code> to log in.</li> </ol>"};
